  "texto": "Move two. The world gets smaller. It started with small comments. 'Your friend Priya seems... jealous of us.' 'Your sister always makes you feel guilty. Have you noticed?' He never said 'don't see them.' He was much smarter than that. He just made every night with friends cost her something. A sigh at the door. A cold dinner. A mood that lasted until Sunday. Then came the rules that were never called rules. 'Just text me when you get there. I worry.' Soon, 'I worry' became 'Who were you with?' And she answered every single time, to avoid the silence that would follow. Six months in, Maya started canceling plans on her own, to keep the peace. Her calendar emptied. Her world shrank. And she called it choosing him. Psychologists call this isolation. And it's not about loneliness. It's about removing every person who could say: 'This isn't normal.' If this is landing, hit like. It helps this reach someone who needs to hear it. Now Maya had no one left to compare notes with. And that's exactly when the third move began.",
